{"step_index":0,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-04T11:23:37Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nYou are a Principal Software Engineer. Set up a clean, production-grade Next.js 15 (App Router) and Node.js/TypeScript architecture for \"OtakuBazaar\", an Amazon/OLX-scale C2C marketplace.\r\n\r\n### Engineering & Clean Code Requirements:\r\n1. **Directory Structure**:\r\n   - Organize using Clean Architecture:\r\n     - `src/domain`: Pure entities, value objects, and repository interfaces (no external dependencies).\r\n     - `src/application`: Use cases, DTOs, and business logic (e.g., `CreateListingUseCase`, `AcceptBargainOfferUseCase`).\r\n     - `src/infrastructure`: Database repositories (Prisma/Drizzle), external APIs (Razorpay, Shiprocket), WebSockets, and cache.\r\n     - `src/presentation`: Next.js pages, API routes, and React components.\r\n2. **Developer Maintainability**:\r\n   - Every file must have a concise header docstring explaining its single responsibility.\r\n   - Every exported function and method must include JSDoc comments detailing params, return types, and potential thrown exceptions so any new engineer can understand and modify it immediately.\r\n   - Strict TypeScript: No `any` types. Centralize shared types in `src/domain/types`.\r\n3. **Multi-Window Sync Foundation**:\r\n   - Implement a client-side `SyncProvider` utilizing the browser's `BroadcastChannel` API combined with a centralized WebSocket hook.\r\n   - If an action occurs in Window A (e.g., an offer is accepted or item is reserved), Window B and Window C must update their local state immediately without a page refresh.\r\n\r\nGenerate the folder structure and complete foundational files for `SyncProvider.tsx`, `useWebSocketSync.ts`, and a sample Use Case with thorough inline comments.\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-09-04T16:53:37+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\n<USER_SETTINGS_CHANGE>\nThe user changed setting `Model Selection` from None to Claude Opus 4.6 (Thinking). No need to comment on this change if the user doesn't ask about it. If reporting what model you are, please use a human readable name instead of the exact string.\n</USER_SETTINGS_CHANGE>"}
