t integrations replacing the TODO stubs. (Status: NOT STARTED / SUGGESTED)\n\n2. User Knowledge\n- **Architecture Choice**: The user approved a 4-layer Clean Architecture (Domain, Application, Infrastructure, Presentation) for OtakuBazaar.\n- **Project Requirements**:\n    - \"Clean, production-grade Next.js 15 (App Router) and Node.js/TypeScript architecture.\"\n    - \"Every file must have a concise header docstring.\"\n    - \"Every exported function and method must include JSDoc comments.\"\n    - \"Strict TypeScript: No `any` types.\"\n    - \"Multi-window sync foundation using `BroadcastChannel` and `WebSocket`.\"\n- **Scope**: The user approved the architectural scaffold approach which includes all interfaces, domain entities, two key use cases (`CreateListingUseCase`, `AcceptBargainOfferUseCase`), sync infrastructure, and API route stubs.\n\n3. Work Accomplished\n- **Project Scaffolding**: Initialized `otaku-bazaar` using Next.js 15 App Router, TypeScript, and ESLint.\n- **Domain Layer**: Fully implemented `Listing`, `BargainOffer`, and `User` entities, `Money` and status value objects, domain events, and repository ports.\n- **Application Layer**: Fully implemented `CreateListingUseCase` and `AcceptBargainOfferUseCase`, typed errors, and infrastructure ports (`IEventBus`, `IPaymentGateway`, `IShippingProvider`).\n- **Infrastructure Layer**: Created `Prisma` schema, `PrismaListingRepository`, `PrismaBargainOfferRepository`, `RazorpayGateway` stub, `ShiprocketProvider` stub, `WebSocketEventBus` stub, and `RedisCache` (in-memory) stub.\n- **Presentation Layer**: Implemented `SyncProvider.tsx`, `useWebSocketSync.ts`, `ListingCard.tsx` component, and API routes for `/api/listings` and `/api/bargain/accept`.\n\n4. Model Knowledge\n- **Architecture & Interfaces**:\n    - Domain aggregates (`Listing`, `BargainOffer`) manage state transitions via domain value objects (`ListingStatus`, `OfferStatus`).\n    - Use cases perform validation, invoke aggregates, persist via repository ports (`IListingRepository`, `IBargainOfferRepository`), and publish events via `IEventBus`.\n    - `SyncProvider` context orchestrates real-time events by subscribing to `WebSocketEventBus` and `BroadcastChannel`.\n- **Sync Pattern**: Cross-device sync uses `WebSocket` (Server -> Client), same-device cross-tab sync uses `BroadcastChannel` (Tab -> Tab). `SyncProvider` acts as the single source of truth for UI components subscribing to these real-time events.\n- **Concurrency**: Repository `update` methods in infrastructure must eventually handle optimistic concurrency (e.g., using Prisma `updatedAt` checks), which is currently identified as a requirement but not fully implemented in the ORM layer.\n\n5. Files and Code\n- **Edited/Created Files** (All in `C:\\Users\\HP\\.gemini\\antigravity-ide\\scratch\\otaku-bazaar\\src\\...`):\n    - `domain/types/index.ts`: Centralized branded types.\n    - `domain/value-objects/*.ts`: Money, ListingStatus, OfferStatus.\n    - `domain/entities/*.ts`: User, Listing, BargainOffer.\n    - `domain/events/DomainEvent.ts`: Discriminated union of business events.\n    - `domain/repositories/*.ts`: IListingRepository, IBargainOfferRepository interfaces.\n    - `application/errors/ApplicationErrors.ts`: Typed error hierarchy.\n    - `application/ports/*.ts`: EventBus, Payment, Shipping ports.\n    - `application/dtos/*.ts`: Listing/Accept DTOs.\n    - `application/use-cases/*.ts`: CreateListing, AcceptBargainOffer logic.\n    - `infrastructure/database/prisma/schema.prisma`: Prisma models.\n    - `infrastructure/database/repositories/*.ts`: Prisma implementations.\n    - `infrastructure/payment/RazorpayGateway.ts`: Payment stub.\n    - `infrastructure/shipping/ShiprocketProvider.ts`: Shipping stub.\n    - `infrastructure/realtime/WebSocketEventBus.ts`: WebSocket event bus.\n    - `infrastructure/cache/RedisCache.ts`: Cache stub.\n    - `presentation/hooks/useWebSocketSync.ts`: WebSocket connection hook.\n    - `presentation/components/providers/SyncProvider.tsx`: Sync context provider.\n    - `presentation/components/listings/ListingCard.tsx`: Sync-enabled UI.\n    - `app/api/listings/route.ts` & `app/api/bargain/accept/route.ts`: API route stubs.\n\n6. Current Work and Next Steps\n- The structural scaffold is complete.\n- Next Steps: The next agent should focus on wiring up Dependency Injection (DI) to replace the `TODO` placeholders in the API route handlers and integrating the Prisma client. Final step is verifying the setup with `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npm run dev`.\n\nYou have the 2 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: implementation_plan]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/HP/.gemini/antigravity-ide/brain/4ef0148b-ff8c-4889-8f54-3ee5a03210d9/implementation_plan.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-04T11:24:58Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: task]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/HP/.gemini/antigravity-ide/brain/4ef0148b-ff8c-4889-8f54-3ee5a03210d9/task.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-04T11:25:40Z\n\n# Conversation Logs\n\nReference the following log files for the full, untruncated conversation:\n\n- C:\\Users\\HP\\.gemini\\antigravity-ide\\brain\\4ef0148b-ff8c-4889-8f54-3ee5a03210d9\\.system_generated\\logs\\transcript.jsonl\n\n**IMPORTANT: this summary is just for your reference. You may respond to my previous and future messages, but DO NOT ACKNOWLEDGE THIS CHECKPOINT MESSAGE. JUST READ IT BUT DO NOT MENTION IT, RESPOND TO IT, OR TAKE ACTION BECAUSE OF IT.**"}
